<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">regions</ansi>

East of Alderbrook the land climbs through a chain of regions, each for a
higher band of levels than the last. A band is the level of the foes you
meet there (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>), so a company at or above a region's band finds it
easy, and one well under it needs careful preparation.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The road, in order</ansi>
  Alderbrook             levels 2-4     the hamlet's fringe: rats, dogs, brigands
  Brindle Downs          levels 4-6     open sheep country with wolves and brigands
  Marrowmere Fen         levels 6-8     marsh: crocodiles, poachers, spiders
  Greywatch Pass         levels 9-11    mountain pass; an ogre lairs at the Gap
  Cinder Hollow          levels 12-14   burnt woods held by ruffians
  Thornreach Wood        levels 15-17   thorn and wolf; an ent in its hollow
  Hollowweb Deep         levels 18-20   spider country; the queen in her den
  Ashen Barrows          levels 21-24   crypts: skeletons, acolytes, a lich
  Glassvault Depths      levels 25-28   caves: stalkers, creepers, an abyssal one
  Stormcrown Heights     levels 29-33   the summit: an ogre and an ent hold the throne
  Each region's west end joins the one before it and its east end the one
  after. At levels 30 and above a character may promote to an elite class
  (<ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What each region offers</ansi>
  Every region has an inn with a hearth (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>) and a clearing or shelf
  where a company can camp, so a rest is never far. Only some rooms spring
  encounters; the inn, camp, and ends of the region never do. Water, game,
  herbs, firewood and shelter are gathered where the room lists them
  (<ansi fg="command">help gathering</ansi>), and the biome decides the weather and cold you face
  (<ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>). The crypts and caves are dark, so carry a light
  (<ansi fg="command">help light</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Lairs and relics</ansi>
  Each boss waits in a lair room marked on the map, at the far end of its
  region. Beat one and it may drop a relic of its own (<ansi fg="command">help relics</ansi>); the
  ogre, the ent, the spider queen, the lich and the abyssal creeper each
  have relics to win, and the summit's throne is held by an ogre or an
  ent, whichever comes.
  A lair falls quiet for your company for about half an hour once beaten
  (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Finds</ansi>
  Two hunters' recipe pages lie in the open: one in a lean-to on Brindle
  Downs and one in a trapper's cache in Marrowmere Fen. <ansi fg="command">use</ansi> a page to learn
  its dish (<ansi fg="command">help recipes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Finding your way</ansi>
  In the web client the map draws each region as tiles; click a tile you
  have visited to walk there (<ansi fg="command">help walkto</ansi>). <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">scout</ansi> name the zone's
  level band and how it weighs on your company.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help relics</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help walkto</ansi>.
